r.cs; python3 .agents/factory/story-gate.py --story pay-through-the-provider --stage document 2>&1 | tail -15","description":"Fix line refs and run the document gate"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_019AtRBHv5KjX6C1Qvg2LZu1","tool_input":{"command":"ls ../planning/porting-status.md; grep -n \"def check_glossary\\|neither in a glossary\" -A40 .agents/factory/story-gate.py | head -90","description":"Inspect gate glossary check logic"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":40,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The document stage for `pay-through-the-provider` is done and every gate check passes. The story now waits for you to accept it: the gate wrote `.agents/factory/decisions/pay-through-the-provider-accept-1.md`, which you answer through `/factory-decisions`. I ran no other stage and committed nothing.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Checkout glossary** (`src/DcaShop.Checkout/Domain/glossary.md`), updated through `ubiquitous-language`:\n  - **New `PaymentOutcome` entry:** a payment is `Succeeded`, `Refused` or `Unavailable`. The plan's \"Payment authorization\" and \"Payment refusal\" became two of its values, because the code has no type by either name.\n  - **Payment failures entry:** \"unavailable\" now also means the provider can't be reached, doesn't answer in time, or answers outside its contract. The entry names the two fixed texts the customer sees. It also corrects the old line that the provider's reason travels through unchanged: the reason still goes into the exception and the log, but not onto the page.\n  - **`PaymentProviderId`:** the shop registers exactly one provider — `provider` (the REST one) when `Checkout:PaymentProvider:BaseUrl` is set, `mock` otherwise.\n- **Designed map** (`project/domain.md`), updated through `context-map`: the Payment Service Provider row and design choice 2 now name `RestPaymentProvider` as the adapter and the stand-in for when no address is set. They no longer say \"in place of a real gateway\". No relationship was added or changed.\n- **`README.md`, `## Run`:** one new paragraph on how to point the shop at a real provider (`Checkout:PaymentProvider:BaseUrl` / `Checkout__PaymentProvider__BaseUrl`) and on the 2-second timeout setting.\n- **Generated context map:** no hand edit. The build stage already regenerated it.\n- **Stage record:** `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/document.md`.\n\n**Left undocumented, with the reasons in `document.md`:**\n- **`project/product.md`:** unchanged. The shipped shop still pays with the stand-in, so \"Real payment\" under \"not part of the product\" still holds. Whether it should come off that list is your call.\n- **Java twin:** its glossary, its designed map and the parent directory's porting status were not checked. That needs a pass across both repositories.\n- **Open design points:** the JSON field names are still an assumption, and the REST provider has no cancellation endpoint.\n\nOn the first gate run, `document.md` cited two paths outside this repository and did not list the plan's proposal labels word for word. I reworded both and the rerun passed.","ttft_ms":2817,"type":"result","duration_ms":167496,"uuid":"a70c3a0d-f418-4965-a8ce-31805972eff1","ttft_stream_ms":1872,"time_to_request_ms":68,"first_content_frame_ms":1872,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
